{
  "tema": 6748,
  "slug": "imperativo-tu-afirmativo",
  "titulo": "Affirmative tú commands",
  "subtitulo": "¡Rema, rema, que viene la ola!",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "For most verbs, the affirmative tú command is the same as the él/ella form of the present: habla, come, escribe. Stem changes stay: cierra, vuelve, pide.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To tell a friend (**tú**) to do something, take the **él/ella form of the present**. That's the command."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "él form of the present",
            "=",
            "tú command"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Infinitive",
            "Él/ella present",
            "Tú command"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "hablar",
              "habla",
              "**¡Habla!**"
            ],
            [
              "comer",
              "come",
              "**¡Come!**"
            ],
            [
              "escribir",
              "escribe",
              "**¡Escribe!**"
            ],
            [
              "cerrar (e → ie)",
              "cierra",
              "**¡Cierra!**"
            ],
            [
              "volver (o → ue)",
              "vuelve",
              "**¡Vuelve!**"
            ],
            [
              "pedir (e → i)",
              "pide",
              "**¡Pide!**"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Stem changes stay**: **piensa**, **duerme**, **sigue**, **riega**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "This is only for **affirmative** commands. Negative tú commands use another form: **no hables**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A handful of very common verbs are irregular (**di, haz, ve, pon, sal, sé, ten, ven**). They have their own lesson."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Habla== más despacio, por favor.",
              "en": "Speak more slowly, please."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Come== algo antes del entrenamiento.",
              "en": "Eat something before training."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Escribe== tu nombre aquí.",
              "en": "Write your name here."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Cierra== la puerta, que hace frío.",
              "en": "Close the door, it's cold."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Vuelve== temprano, mañana hay clase.",
              "en": "Come back early, there's class tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Riega== las plantas en la tarde.",
              "en": "Water the plants in the afternoon."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Pide== la cuenta, ya nos vamos.",
              "en": "Ask for the check, we're leaving."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Rema==, rema, que viene la ola!",
              "en": "Paddle, paddle, here comes the wave!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
